  "summary": "Apple products with proven secondary-market resale. Aliases are deliberately specific (e.g., 'apple tv 4k' NOT bare 'apple tv') to avoid matching the dead-tier products like 2nd/3rd gen Apple TV that no longer get app support and have near-zero resale. Skip-list is a backup safety net for any older-gen titles that slip through. Rule of thumb for Apple resale: Mac with Apple Silicon (M1+, 2020+) ≫ Intel Mac. iPhone 12+ ≫ older. Apple Watch Series 7+ ≫ older. iPad Pro/Air ≫ base iPad. Be skeptical of anything pre-2018.",
  "field_workflow": [
    "Always verify model identifier on the device itself — boxes alone aren't enough",
    "Check Activation Lock status (iCloud locked = nearly worthless)",
    "Battery health is the single biggest resale driver for portables (MacBook, iPhone, iPad)",
    "Run About This Mac / Settings → General → About to confirm chip generation",
    "AppleCare+ remaining transferable to buyer — premium",
    "Original box / cables / accessories add 10-20% premium",
    "Cosmetic dings on aluminum bodies are visible and impact resale heavily"
  ],
